Turen Browser Artifacts is a bounded, offline WebAssembly parser for browser
forensic artifacts: Chromium LevelDB write logs (.log, used by Local Storage,
Session Storage, and IndexedDB), Chromium LevelDB tables (.ldb/.sst),
Chromium simple-disk-cache entry files, and Safari Cookies.binarycookies
jars. The wrapper, dispatch/bounding layer, and all four format decoders are
original Turen code written against documented on-disk formats (LevelDB
log_format/table_format, Chromium net/disk_cache/simple entry format,
WebKit-compatible binarycookies layout). No upstream application code is
included. Licensed Apache-2.0 OR MIT.

This package vendors compiled third-party Rust components:

- snap 1.1.1 — BSD-3-Clause (Andrew Gallant / BurntSushi). Pure-Rust Snappy
  raw-block decompression for LevelDB table blocks; decompressed size is
  bounded before allocation.
- crc32c 0.6.8 — Apache-2.0 OR MIT. CRC-32C (Castagnoli) checksums for
  LevelDB record and table-block integrity; the software table
  implementation is used on wasm32.
- serde 1.0.228 and serde_json 1.0.151 — MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- sha2 0.10.9 — MIT OR Apache-2.0 (RustCrypto). Used for cache-entry key
  SHA-256 validation and record digests.
- wasm-bindgen 0.2.108 — MIT OR Apache-2.0.

Transitive components of the above are distributed under permissive MIT,
